  "raw_text": "A key reframing dissolved the assumption that local hardware was a blocker for processing the first corpus. Because the pipeline routed operators to local models only to honor the privacy non-negotiable, and the first corpus is published Innocence Project / DNA exoneration court records that are public, the privacy gate does not bite on that data and claude -p is a legitimate substrate. The private affidavits are deliberately sequenced last, so the hardware-versus-local question becomes real only at the calibration end. The actual near-term constraint was therefore identified as the subscription's rate window, not privacy, hardware, or per-call cost.",
